    <briefdescription>
<para>Volumetric-deviatoric (V-D) split and projection tensors of the microplane theory, as used e.g. by damage-plasticity constitutive microplane models. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The macroscopic strain is decomposed on each microplane into a volumetric part <formula id="320">$ \varepsilon_V = \tfrac{1}{3}\operatorname{tr}(\eps) $</formula>, identical for every microplane, and a deviatoric microplane strain vector <formula id="321">$ \eps_D $</formula>. <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_v_d_split_1adbb2263b6b70c4eddc969cf930438bb7" kindref="member">pTensors</ref> holds the corresponding projection tensors (<ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_v_d_split_1_1projection_tensors_1a3dd8120ac7e5d892b7532e18d90adf0f" kindref="member">Marmot::ContinuumMechanics::Microplane::VDSplit::projectionTensors::Vol</ref>, <ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_v_d_split_1_1projection_tensors_1a23d8ec887f3ed5f5d65ea8ca838a28a7" kindref="member">Marmot::ContinuumMechanics::Microplane::VDSplit::projectionTensors::Dev</ref>) built from the hard-coded discretization (Discretization::get()), and the <computeroutput>homogenize*</computeroutput> methods perform the virtual-work homogenization of per-microplane volumetric/deviatoric quantities back to macroscopic 3x3 tensors. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>scheme</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The <ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1af92b719bb2e032a4645d5e37f808cbd1" kindref="member">QuadratureScheme</ref> (and thus the number of microplanes <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_v_d_split_1a327036017ea8910dc16ab96b6472ea6c" kindref="member">nqp</ref>) this instantiation is built for. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
